  "name": "hotosm_lva_waterways",
  "notes": "Water features across the region from OSM. Includes rivers, streams, canals, lakes, ponds, and water bodies tagged with `waterway`, `water`, or `natural=water`. Useful for flood-risk modelling, watershed analysis, and environmental basemap context.\n\nOpenStreetMap is a free, collaborative world map built by volunteers. Completeness varies by region: urban areas are usually well-mapped, remote areas may be incomplete. Cross-check critical decisions with local field knowledge.\n\n- Source: [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org)\n- OSM tags: [Key:waterway](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:waterway), [Key:water](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:water), [Key:natural](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:natural)\n- Part of many  [exports grid on HDX](https://data.humdata.org/organization/hot) by the [HOT](https://www.hotosm.org/en/)\n",
